# Offline shader compatibility experiment (3 October 2026)

- User constraint: game closed, do not launch it; investigate shader translation and deploy a reversible bottle experiment. (3 October 2026)
- Previous runtime evidence already proves D3DMetal 3.0 was loaded, with the D3DMetal shader cache open. DirectX 12 translation and DXR compatibility are separate; no evidence supports saying the previous crash came from absence of D3DMetal. (3 October 2026)
- All 141 shader archives remain hash-identical; 1257 DXBC/DXIL containers have valid structural bounds and LLVM magic. This does not validate every instruction, resource binding or rendered pixel. The verifier rejects a deliberately truncated container. (3 October 2026)
- Standardmaterial and gpupipe_material expose 38 extracted containers accepted by the installed Apple converter. Five compile standalone; 33 request a root signature (errorCode 1). That context is normally supplied by the game, so this result does not show a broken shader. (3 October 2026)
- The inventory includes Shader Model 6.9 in six shader archives, mainly RT-related plus deferredlight_volume. Presence alone does not prove a currently selected permutation or unsupported execution. (3 October 2026)
- Inspection of the actual D3DMetal binary shows D3DM_BOUNDS_CHECK and D3DM_SAMPLE_NAN_TO_ZERO default to true. Enabling either would repeat the default and is not deployed as a fix. (3 October 2026)
- D3DM_FORCE_RTZ_TEXWRITE is read with getenv/atoi, defaults to false, is stored at configuration offset 0x552 and feeds compatibility bit 6 to IRCompilerSetCompatibilityFlags. Changing this bit on five standalone compilable material shaders succeeds in both modes and changes Metal output hashes for four. The flag name suggests rounding toward zero on texture writes; the precise visual consequence is not established. (3 October 2026)
- Applied only under the bottle EnvironmentVariables: CX_GRAPHICS_BACKEND=d3dmetal, D3DM_FORCE_RTZ_TEXWRITE=1. Preserved existing MetalFX and renderer.ini; RT/PT settings remain zero. No CrossOver framework, game executable, original shader or driver is replaced. (3 October 2026)
- The actual 66 MB D3DMetal shaders.cache directory is moved to the backup named in ShaderCompatibilityPatch.json; all archived file hashes are verified. This prepares a fresh cache at the next user launch, but has not compiled the game's live pipelines yet. (3 October 2026)
- Rollback is tested: configuration and every original cache file return byte-identical, then the experiment is reapplied. Evidence: ShaderCompatibilityRollbackTest.json. (3 October 2026)
- Next validation, only when the user launches: confirm D3DMetal loaded, let cache rebuild, revisit the same affected windows, capture static color and camera-motion stability. If unchanged, test cache rebuild without RTZ separately using the rollback command. No successful window-render claim exists yet. (3 October 2026)

